---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **작품은 줄었는데 자리는 안 줄었다.** (`/fewer-titles`)
 *
 * ── 왜 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   넷플릭스가 2026년 한국 작품 슬레이트를 키운다고 냈다. 우리 차트는 반대로 갔다 —
 *   차트에 오른 작품이 276(2022) → 203(2025). 그런데 **자리는 안 줄었다.**
 *   ⭐ 그러면 물음은 「누가 그 자리를 가져갔나」다. 답은 **한 편**이다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **작품당 자리 하나로 말하지 않는다.** 두 수의 나눗셈이라 어느 쪽이 움직였는지 못 가린다.
 *    그래서 작품 수·자리 수를 따로 내고, 윗 열 편 몫은 **가장 큰 한 편을 빼고** 한 번 더 낸다.
 * ⛔ **둘째·셋째를 안 적는다.** 가장 큰 한 편은 사실이고, 그 뒤를 적는 순간 순위표가 된다.
 * ⛔ 덜 찬 해(2021·2026)를 견줌에 안 섞는다. 화면에 「덜 찬 해」라고 적는다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 * ⚠ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `wikitip-fewer-titles.json` 에서 읽는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-fewer-titles.json';

const 첫 = d.byYear.find((y) => y.year === d.firstFullYear);
const 끝 = d.byYear.find((y) => y.year === d.lastFullYear);
const 온전 = d.byYear.filter((y) => y.weeks >= 40);

const TITLE = 'Fewer Korean titles chart every year. The places they hold have not fallen';
const DESC =
  `${첫.titles} Korean titles reached a Netflix country top 10 in ${첫.year} and ${끝.titles} in `
  + `${끝.year}, a fall of ${Math.abs(d.titlesChangePc)}%, while the places they held rose `
  + `${d.placesChangePc}%. Remove each year's biggest title and the ten largest gained `
  + `${(d.topTenWithoutBiggestLast - d.topTenWithoutBiggestFirst).toFixed(1)} points instead of `
  + `${(d.topTenLast - d.topTenFirst).toFixed(1)}.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10', 'https://www.wikidata.org'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/fewer-titles">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  {/* ⛔ 요약값을 지면에서 다시 셈하지 않는다. 두 곳에서 셈하면 언젠가 어긋나고, 어긋난 쪽이 화면에 나간다 */}
  <p class="q">
    {d.titlesFirst} titles in {d.firstFullYear} · <b>{d.titlesLast}</b> in {d.lastFullYear} —
    {' '}{Math.abs(d.titlesChangePc)}% fewer. Places held: {d.placesFirst.toLocaleString('en-US')} →{' '}
    <b>{d.placesLast.toLocaleString('en-US')}</b>, up {d.placesChangePc}%.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Same shelf, a quarter fewer titles on it</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Year</th><th>Titles that charted</th><th>Chart places held</th><th>Places per title</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.byYear.map((y) => (
            <tr class={y.weeks < 40 ? 'part' : undefined}>
              <td class="nm">{y.year}{y.weeks < 40 && <span class="fine"> — part year, {y.weeks} weeks</span>}</td>
              <td>{y.titles}</td>
              <td>{y.places.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td class="tot">{y.placesPerTitle}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      <b>{d.unit}</b>
    </p>
    <p class="warn">
      <b>Distrust the last column.</b> {d.whyNotPlacesPerTitle}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>So where did the places go</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Year</th><th>Ten biggest titles hold</th>
            <th>Same, biggest title removed</th><th>Outside the top ten, per title</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {온전.map((y) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{y.year}</td>
              <td>{y.topTenPc}%</td>
              <td class="tot">{y.topTenPcWithoutBiggest}%</td>
              <td>{y.restPlacesPerTitle}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      {d.whyWithoutBiggest}
    </p>
    <p class="q">
      With the biggest title in: <b>{(d.topTenLast - d.topTenFirst).toFixed(1)} points</b>.
      With it out: <b>{(d.topTenWithoutBiggestLast - d.topTenWithoutBiggestFirst).toFixed(1)} points</b>.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      And the rest of the field barely moved: a title outside the ten biggest held{' '}
      {d.restPerTitleFirst} places in {첫.year} and {d.restPerTitleLast} in {끝.year}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The concentration is one title</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Biggest single title</th><th>Its share of all Korean chart places</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.byYear.filter((y) => y.year !== '2026').map((y) => (
            <tr class={y.weeks < 40 ? 'part' : undefined}>
              <td class="nm">{y.year}{y.weeks < 40 && <span class="fine"> — part year</span>}</td>
              <td>{y.biggestTitle}</td>
              <td class="tot">{y.topOnePc}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="q">
      The biggest title of the year held <b>{d.topOneFirst}%</b> of all Korean chart places in{' '}
      {d.firstFullYear} and <b>{d.topOneLast}%</b> in {d.lastFullYear}.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>We do not name a second or a third.</b> One title holding a quarter of a year's places is a
      fact about the shape of the chart. A list of the ones behind it would be a ranking, and this
      publication does not print those.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      The smallest band moved too: titles that took five chart places or fewer in a whole year fell
      from <b>{d.tinyFirst}</b> to <b>{d.tinyLast}</b>. That is {첫.titles - 끝.titles} fewer titles
      charting in total, and the places did not follow them out.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>How this was counted, and what it cannot say</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Source</b> — {d.source}</li>
      <li><b>Rows read</b> — {d.rowsRead.toLocaleString('en-US')}.</li>
      <li><b>Part years</b> — {d.partialYears.join(' and ')} are shown but excluded from every
        comparison. The trend is read from {d.firstFullYear} to {d.lastFullYear}.</li>
      <li><b>Seasons count as their show.</b> Netflix lists seasons separately; counted separately, a
        returning show would look like several new titles — which is the thing being measured here.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="warn">{d.cannotAnswer}</p>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/leverage">Did the charts concentrate by company</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/clumping">Why 7.7% is not one place a week</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/exit">How a title leaves</a> · <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/fewer-titles" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  tr.part td { opacity: 0.62; }
</style>
